    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "https://www.auctioneera.ie/property/243-cashel-road-crumlin-dublin-d12-vf7y\r\nImportant note: Details of upcoming viewings and latest offers are available at the Auctioneera website link above.\r\n\r\nAuctioneera is delighted to present 243 Cashel Road, Crumlin in Dublin.\r\n\r\nPositioned at the end of an established terrace, 243 Cashel Road is a practical two-bedroom home with a rendered exterior, gated front garden and covered entrance porch. A modest lawn and paved pathway lead to the front door, creating a neat and welcoming approach to the property. On-street parking is available directly outside and within the immediate area.\r\n\r\nUpon entering, the hallway leads to a comfortable front sitting room featuring a broad window and traditional fireplace. To the rear, the kitchen forms part of a bright and versatile living space, with fitted cabinetry, practical worktop space and room for both seating and everyday dining. A large window overlooks the rear garden and brings natural light into the room.\r\n\r\nAdjoining the kitchen is a compact utility and storage area equipped with laundry facilities and useful shelving. This area also provides direct access to the rear garden, adding to the practicality of the ground-floor layout.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the property provides two well-proportioned bedrooms. The larger bedroom benefits from fitted wardrobe storage, a feature fireplace and a generous window, while the second bedroom offers flexibility for sleeping accommodation, guest use or a home office. The bathroom is fitted with a bath, wash-hand basin and WC.\r\n\r\nThe sizeable rear garden is primarily laid to lawn and bordered by established planting. A paved section provides space for outdoor seating, while the sheds and outbuildings offer useful garden storage. As an end-of-terrace home, the property also benefits from gated side access to the rear. The overall space offers scope for gardening, relaxation or outdoor entertaining.\r\n\r\nThe property is well served by local bus routes and enjoys convenient access to a range of everyday amenities. Schools are within walking distance, while Ashleaf Shopping Centre and the nearby Carlisle gym provide convenient shopping and leisure options. Terenure and Rathmines are also accessible on foot, placing a wider selection of shops, cafés and services within reach.\r\n\r\n243 Cashel Road offers a well-arranged layout, two distinct living areas, useful utility space and a generous rear garden. Its end-of-terrace position, convenient bus connections and established residential location make it an appealing option for purchasers seeking a manageable home with practical accommodation and outdoor space."
